    "https://www.lec.edu/career-development": {
      "title": "Career Services & Workforce Development",
      "description": "Career Development | Lake Erie College top of page Search Apply Give VISIT Make a Payment LEO More Use tab to navigate through the menu items. Menu Close About History News and Announcements Faculty & Staff Board of Directors Accreditation Events Admissions Campus Tours Tuition & Fees Housing & Dining Financial Aid College Credit Plus (CCP) Office of Veterans and Military Service New Student Orientation Academics Academic Calendar Undergraduate Degrees Graduate Degrees Physician Assistant Program (PA) Study Abroad Partnerships & Pre-Professional Programs Professional Teacher Pathway Registrar Student Life Clubs & Organizations Tower Honors Program Career Development Career Closet Lincoln Learning Commons Campus Safety Non-Degree Programs Professional Development for Teachers Equine Studies Athletics Arts & Culture Alumni & Friends Parents & Family Careers Facilities Bookstore Campus Gear LAKE ERIE ONLINE Career Services & Workforce Development Empowering Students for Purpose-Driven Careers Lake Erie College is proud to introduce its new Career Services and Workforce Development Department — a major step forward in helping students prepare for meaningful, purpose-driven careers. ​ What We Offer Career Services & Workforce Development equips students with the tools, resources, and connections to succeed through: Personalized career coaching and advising Career education integrated into academic programs Strong employer partnerships for internships, mentoring, and job placements Professional preparation for today’s competitive job market Alumni engagement and networking opportunities ​ Nonprofit & Civic Engagement In collaboration with the Nonprofit and Civic Engagement Initiative, Lake Erie College is expanding its regional impact and supporting service-oriented careers through: Workforce development for the nonprofit sector Capacity building for community organizations Civic engagement and public leadership programs Professional education, credentialing, and the annual Nonprofit Summit Strategic partnerships across Northeast Ohio and beyond Visit Us The Career Services and Workforce Development Office is located on the second floor of the Lincoln Learning Commons. Hours: Wednesdays, 1:30–3:00 p.m. | Thursdays, 9:30–11:30 a.m. (or by appointment) ​ Schedule Appointment Visit Campus Overview Apply Request Info 391 W Washington St, Painesville, Ohio, 44077 440.375.7000 © 2026 Lake Erie College Campus Map Catalog and School Handbook Compliments and Complaints Consumer Information Make a Payment APPLY VISIT Give Lake Erie Online bottom of page"
    },
    "https://www.lec.edu/career-closet": {
      "title": "Career Closet",
      "description": "Career Closet | Lake Erie College top of page Search Apply Give VISIT Make a Payment LEO More Use tab to navigate through the menu items. Menu Close About History News and Announcements Faculty & Staff Board of Directors Accreditation Events Admissions Campus Tours Tuition & Fees Housing & Dining Financial Aid College Credit Plus (CCP) Office of Veterans and Military Service New Student Orientation Academics Academic Calendar Undergraduate Degrees Graduate Degrees Physician Assistant Program (PA) Study Abroad Partnerships & Pre-Professional Programs Professional Teacher Pathway Registrar Student Life Clubs & Organizations Tower Honors Program Career Development Career Closet Lincoln Learning Commons Campus Safety Non-Degree Programs Professional Development for Teachers Equine Studies Athletics Arts & Culture Alumni & Friends Parents & Family Careers Facilities Bookstore Campus Gear LAKE ERIE ONLINE Career Closet at Lake Erie college What is the Career Closet? At Lake Erie College, preparing students for success goes beyond the classroom. The Career Closet is a resource designed to help students feel confident, prepared, and professional as they take the next steps in their careers. The Career Closet provides free professional clothing to Lake Erie College students. Whether preparing for interviews, presentations, internships, or networking events, students have access to attire that helps them make a strong first impression. ​ This initiative removes a common barrier to career readiness by ensuring that all students—regardless of financial circumstances—can present themselves with confidence in professional settings. ​ What You’ll Find The Career Closet offers a variety of professional clothing options, including: Dress shirts and blouses Pants and skirts Blazers and sport coats Business casual and professional attire Accessories such as belts Students can browse and select items at no cost. ​ How to Support Community members can support the Career Closet through donations. Current needs include: Women's professional clothing: Dress pants, skirts, blouses, blazers,  dresses, shoes Men's Professional Clothing: Pants, sport coats, shoes, button down shirts ​ Every contribution—big or small—makes a meaningful impact on a student’s confidence and career journey. ​ Schedule Appointment Donate to Career Closet Visit Campus Overview Apply Request Info 391 W Washington St, Painesville, Ohio, 44077 440.375.7000 © 2026 Lake Erie College Campus Map Catalog and School Handbook Compliments and Complaints Consumer Information Make a Payment APPLY VISIT Give Lake Erie Online bottom of page"
    },
    "https://www.lec.edu/career-and-professional-advancement-programs": {
      "title": "Non-Degree Programs",
      "description": "Non-Degree Programs | Lake Erie College top of page Search Apply Give VISIT Make a Payment LEO More Use tab to navigate through the menu items. Menu Close About History News and Announcements Faculty & Staff Board of Directors Accreditation Events Admissions Campus Tours Tuition & Fees Housing & Dining Financial Aid College Credit Plus (CCP) Office of Veterans and Military Service New Student Orientation Academics Academic Calendar Undergraduate Degrees Graduate Degrees Physician Assistant Program (PA) Study Abroad Partnerships & Pre-Professional Programs Professional Teacher Pathway Registrar Student Life Clubs & Organizations Tower Honors Program Career Development Career Closet Lincoln Learning Commons Campus Safety Non-Degree Programs Professional Development for Teachers Equine Studies Athletics Arts & Culture Alumni & Friends Parents & Family Careers Facilities Bookstore Campus Gear LAKE ERIE ONLINE Non-Degree Programs Career and Professional Advancement at Lake Erie College At Lake Erie College, we know that every career journey is unique. Our Career and Professional Advancement Programs are designed to help you gain new skills, strengthen your resume, and grow in your field. ​ Applied Technical Skills Develop hands-on technical expertise. Our 11-month evening HVACR Technician Certification Program—offered through the National Coalition of Certification Centers (NC3)—prepares working professionals to enter or advance in the HVACR industry. ​ Applied Professional Skills Enhance your workplace communication and leadership abilities. Our upcoming Conflict and Negotiation Skills Mastery Module is a fully online, non-credit course ideal for professionals seeking advancement or recent graduates building their resumes. Participants earn a certificate of completion. ​ Advanced Skills for Teachers Teachers can expand their expertise through graduate-level Professional Development Programs offered by the Center for Professional Development. Courses—taught by experienced K–12 educators—support license renewal and classroom innovation, with flexible options including pass/fail credit and independent study. ​ helpful links to Tailor your education experience Academic Calendar Tower Honors Program Study Abroad Partnerships and Accelerated Programs Office of Student Life HVACR HVACR Certification Conflict Management, Negotiation, & Organizational Dynamics Professional Development for Teachers Lake Erie College’s Center for Professional Development supports the ongoing needs of K–12 educators through nearly 100 graduate-level professional development (PD) courses. ​ Whether you’re an administrator renewing your license, a teacher earning graduate credits to move up the pay scale, or a licensed educator not currently teaching, Lake Erie offers flexible, relevant courses designed for you.​ ​ Courses are taught by experienced educators, all with master’s degrees or higher, who bring real classroom expertise to every session. Our technology courses focus on practical strategies for integrating tech to enhance teaching and learning—all offered at a competitive tuition rate with personalized support. ​ Contact us to learn more about upcoming offerings and registration details. ​ View Certifications ODE Five-Year License IDS Meet the professional development staff and Faculty Greg Rothwell, PhD Dean of the School of Education, Assistant Professor of Education Title IX Investigator Phone 1 (440) 375-7371 Mail grothwell@lec.edu Location Garfield Center About Dr. Rothwell ​ Greg Rothwell is currently the Program Director of Education & Professional Studies. Previously, he has served as assistant and head principal of Follansbee Middle School and Brooke High School, in Brooke County, West Virginia. Before his career in administrative positions, Greg taught history at Brooke High School. During his tenure at Brooke High School, Greg served on numerous committees including groups focusing on curriculum and technology, establishing many Advanced Placement courses, and academic-based competition teams. Also, Greg has served in many leadership roles, including the Brooke High School faculty senate chair, social studies department chair, member of the school leadership team, local school improvement council, and a regional advisory committee for professional development. As a leader, Greg has established an emphasis on STEM education at the district level, working with curriculum directors and faculty. After receiving grant money, Greg and his team traveled throughout the country to learn about STEM-related educational techniques and technologies. Greg earned his Ph.D. from Robert Morris University in Moon Township, Pennsylvania, studying Instructional Management and Leadership. His dissertation title is \"An Updated Look at Adopters and Non-Adopters of Educational Technology Among Teachers in a Rural Setting\". He has also earned an M.A in Teaching and Learning with Technology from Ashford University (IA), an M.A in Educational Leadership from Wheeling Jesuit University (WV), and a B.A. in Secondary Education with an emphasis on social studies from West Liberty University (WV). ​ Prepare for a rewarding, high-demand career in Heating, Ventilation, Air Conditioning, and Refrigeration (HVACR) with hands-on, expert-led training at Lake Erie College. ​ Our five-semester program, built on the nationally recognized ESCO Institute curriculum, provides the technical skills and certifications employers value most. Students train in a state-of-the-art HVAC suite, gain experience with modern controls and technology, and receive entry-level tools valued at over $1,000 upon certification. ​ Certifications Earned 30-Hour OSHA Safety Certification ESCO Electrical Certificate ESCO Gas Heating Certificate ESCO Combustion Analysis & Fuel Efficiency Certificate EPA Section 608 Certification & License ​ Financial Support Scholarships and financial aid are available to help make your HVACR career goals a reality. Request Info or Apply for a Scholarship today to start your journey toward a high-demand technical career. ​ Apply for HVACR Program School of Business | 100% Online Lake Erie College is proud to introduce a new fully online graduate certificate designed for working professionals. Equip yourself with the advanced skills needed to effectively manage conflict, lead difficult conversations, and navigate complex corporate environments. ​ Program Highlights 100% Online & Flexible: Completed in just one year via convenient 7-week course formats. Fast-Track to a Degree: All 12 credits can be applied directly as electives toward a Lake Erie College MBA or Master of Professional Studies (MPS). Affordable Tuition: Benefit from an introductory rate of $1,000 per course (over 50% off standard graduate tuition). Total Credits: 12 credit hours (4 courses). ​ Program Curriculum The curriculum consists of four sequential, 3-credit courses focused on real-world application: Conflict Dynamics in Organizations: Power, Identity, and Culture Explore the root causes of workplace conflict and learn frameworks to analyze and diagnose them. Strategic Communication and Difficult Conversations Master communication strategies for high-stakes interactions, active listening, and effective feedback. Negotiation and Influence in Organizations Dive into negotiation theory, integrative approaches, and strategic decision-making. Mediation and Conflict Resolution Practice Build hands-on skills through interactive simulations and structured dispute-resolution frameworks. ​ Admissions Requirements A minimum 3.0 GPA OR relevant industry experience. ​ ​ Apply Meet the Faculty Dr. Aibak Hafeez, Ph.D., M.HRIR, M.Phil. Assistant Professor, Mediator, Arbitrator Mail ahafeez@lec.edu Location College Hall The program is spearheaded by Dr. Aibak Hafeez, a nationally recognized conflict management scholar, mediator, and arbitrator. ​ Education: Ph.D. from the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign; Postdoctoral training at Cornell University’s Scheinman Institute. Real-World Expertise: Active mediator with the U.S. Equal Employment Opportunity Commission (EEOC) and arbitrator with the Financial Industry Regulatory Authority (FINRA). ​ “Today’s organizations demand leaders who can navigate complexity, manage conflict, and communicate effectively under pressure. This program bridges theory and practice to give professionals the tools and confidence to handle high-stakes interactions.” — Dr. Aibak Hafeez, Program Lead Office of Financial Aid Visit Campus Overview Apply Request Info 391 W Washington St, Painesville, Ohio, 44077 440.375.7000 © 2026 Lake Erie College Campus Map Catalog and School Handbook Compliments and Complaints Consumer Information Make a Payment APPLY VISIT Give Lake Erie Online bottom of page"
    },
    "https://www.lec.edu/careers": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers | Lake Erie College top of page Search Apply Give VISIT Make a Payment LEO More Use tab to navigate through the menu items. Menu Close About History News and Announcements Faculty & Staff Board of Directors Accreditation Events Admissions Campus Tours Tuition & Fees Housing & Dining Financial Aid College Credit Plus (CCP) Office of Veterans and Military Service New Student Orientation Academics Academic Calendar Undergraduate Degrees Graduate Degrees Physician Assistant Program (PA) Study Abroad Partnerships & Pre-Professional Programs Professional Teacher Pathway Registrar Student Life Clubs & Organizations Tower Honors Program Career Development Career Closet Lincoln Learning Commons Campus Safety Non-Degree Programs Professional Development for Teachers Equine Studies Athletics Arts & Culture Alumni & Friends Parents & Family Careers Facilities Bookstore Campus Gear LAKE ERIE ONLINE Careers Working at Lake Erie College Lake Erie College’s faculty and staff are central to creating an inclusive, supportive, and highly personalized campus experience that encourages student growth and self-discovery. ​ With a small, close-knit campus community, students benefit from meaningful connections with professors and staff who are deeply invested in their success. Guided by the College’s institutional principles of hope, care, and self-discovery, our dedicated faculty and staff form the foundation of an exceptional and transformative collegiate experience. ​ Quick Links and Resources Current Openings Faculty Handbook Employee Handbook SharePoint Service Desk Requests Office of Human Resources Rachel Hanni Vice President for HR & Operations Leslie Ray Director of HR Mackenzie Meeker HR Graduate Assistant Visit Campus Overview Apply Request Info 391 W Washington St, Painesville, Ohio, 44077 440.375.7000 © 2026 Lake Erie College Campus Map Catalog and School Handbook Compliments and Complaints Consumer Information Make a Payment APPLY VISIT Give Lake Erie Online bottom of page"
